261
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:55,680
Don't worry, I won't.

262
00:15:55,780 --> 00:15:59,500
I wasn't ready before, but now
there's no way I'm gonna lose.

263
00:15:59,720 --> 00:16:01,661
I'll eradicate every one of them.

264
00:16:03,940 --> 00:16:04,770
Let's go.

265
00:16:04,940 --> 00:16:06,420
Right, we're out of here.

266
00:16:25,100 --> 00:16:27,360
Hey, Suzy Q! Look over here!

267
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:31,080
It's goodbye for now, Suzy Q.

268
00:16:31,660 --> 00:16:34,997
I don't know when or how, but
I'll be back in Venice one day.

269
00:16:35,080 --> 00:16:35,910
I promise!

270
00:16:36,820 --> 00:16:37,650
Really?

271
00:16:37,900 --> 00:16:38,730
Yeah.

272
00:16:39,220 --> 00:16:42,926
Peel those ugly wounds on your
face before I get back, will ya?

273
00:16:47,460 --> 00:16:48,290
Later!

274
00:16:49,360 --> 00:16:51,180
Jojo, be careful!

275
00:16:51,740 --> 00:16:54,269
Make sure you come back
in one piece, okay?

276
00:16:54,720 --> 00:16:55,820
Don't get pushy!

277
00:16:56,040 --> 00:16:59,600
You may be an old lady before
I get back, but I will return.

278
00:17:01,700 --> 00:17:02,580
Oh, yeah?

279
00:17:03,320 --> 00:17:04,780
You're a stupid jerk!

280
00:17:15,060 --> 00:17:17,472
I'll be back a lot sooner than you think.

281
00:18:03,360 --> 00:18:04,760
Screams

282
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:09,020
Hey, it drives a damned car, really? Huh?

283
00:18:09,240 --> 00:18:10,917
What's happened to your arms, man?

284
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:11,830
Huh?

285
00:18:12,720 --> 00:18:14,117
Something's wrong with the wheel, man.

286
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:15,553
I can't get it to move.

287
00:18:21,060 --> 00:18:21,890
Hmm.

288
00:18:21,973 --> 00:18:23,340
ACDC hasn't reported back.

289
00:18:23,720 --> 00:18:27,661
He last said that he had learned
the stone was somewhere in Venice.

290
00:18:27,860 --> 00:18:30,331
I wonder if something has happened to him.

291
00:18:33,720 --> 00:18:35,100
Hey, Jojo. Jojo.

292
00:18:37,320 --> 00:18:38,460
Jojo, wake up!

293
00:18:41,080 --> 00:18:43,256
Jojo, we've caught up with the train.

294
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:46,337
They're going through their
customs check at the moment.

295
00:18:46,420 --> 00:18:47,832
That works in our favor.

296
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:52,517
We're less than an hour from San Moritz,
which leaves us enough time to get ready.

297
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:54,040
It's good we caught up.

298
00:18:54,340 --> 00:18:56,240
Come on, Jojo. Look sharp.

299
00:18:57,420 --> 00:19:00,897
Listen, I'm just saving up my strength
for the big battle, that's all.

300
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:02,360
Get off my case!

301
00:19:02,980 --> 00:19:05,897
Let's hurry up and get there
so we can retrieve that stone.

302
00:19:05,980 --> 00:19:09,437
Then we're going to need some sort
of plan for the fight with Wamu.

303
00:19:09,520 --> 00:19:11,700
We'll wait for that until we cross.

304
00:19:14,940 --> 00:19:16,100
What the hell?

305
00:19:17,520 --> 00:19:18,460
Knock it off!

306
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:21,739
If you want to go on, just
quit honking and pass us.

307
00:19:22,740 --> 00:19:28,100
German soldiers What the hell are they
doing in a car on the Swiss-Italian border?

308
00:19:30,960 --> 00:19:33,340
Well, well, you're looking rather spry.

309
00:19:33,860 --> 00:19:37,460
My, you have grown so much, Joestar. Huh?

310
00:19:37,940 --> 00:19:39,411
What did you say, mister?

311
00:19:41,580 --> 00:19:42,900
What was that about?

312
00:19:43,660 --> 00:19:44,840
Get back here!

313
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:46,640
Who the hell are you?

314
00:19:46,860 --> 00:19:47,837
What's going on?

315
00:19:47,920 --> 00:19:49,837
I don't know any German soldiers.

316
00:19:49,920 --> 00:19:51,340
Hey, look at the train!

317
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:53,340
So many soldiers.

318
00:19:54,200 --> 00:19:56,141
Hey, Major, we found the package!

319
00:19:56,580 --> 00:19:57,580
The crest.

320
00:19:58,040 --> 00:19:59,637
Look, they've got the package.

321
00:19:59,720 --> 00:20:01,838
Yeah, and we all know what's inside.

322
00:20:07,760 --> 00:20:09,480
The Red Stone of Asia!

323
00:20:09,800 --> 00:20:11,037
I don't understand.

324
00:20:11,120 --> 00:20:12,708
Why do the Germans want it?

325
00:20:12,880 --> 00:20:15,157
We have decided to take this stone as a

326
00:20:15,240 --> 00:20:17,757
specimen for our scientific
research program.

327
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:20,100
For the past three weeks,

328
00:20:20,320 --> 00:20:24,537
we have been watching your every move
while you were operating in Venice.

329
00:20:24,620 --> 00:20:28,060
We began the surveillance
when we lost our team in Rome.

330
00:20:28,660 --> 00:20:34,000
We saw your training, we saw ACDC, and
we knew you were chasing the stone.

331
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:39,960
Now, our base is set up at
a lodge up ahead. Follow us.

332
00:20:40,640 --> 00:20:44,680
We want to ask a few questions
about the stone and about cars.

333
00:20:45,120 --> 00:20:47,097
Why not work together, eh?

334
00:20:47,180 --> 00:20:50,720
After all, we are not
complete strangers, Jojo.

335
00:20:51,280 --> 00:20:52,110
Hey!

336
00:20:52,193 --> 00:20:53,765
What are you blabbering about?

337
00:20:53,940 --> 00:20:56,697
Don't think you know anything
about me, you bastard!

338
00:20:56,780 --> 00:20:59,377
If the Germans are here, that means...

339
00:20:59,460 --> 00:21:00,700
What do we do, Koch?

340
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:02,980
We have to follow them.

341
00:21:03,500 --> 00:21:06,794
At least we know Crazy doesn't
have the Redstone, either.

342
00:21:07,380 --> 00:21:10,733
At that time, the German army
was marching across Europe,

343
00:21:10,820 --> 00:21:12,197
taking country after country.

344
00:21:12,280 --> 00:21:16,868
They wanted to ensure their rule across
the continent would last indefinitely.

345
00:21:17,320 --> 00:21:20,397
The power of the Mask and
Redstone would solve their problem

346
00:21:20,480 --> 00:21:24,186
perfectly by giving them everything
they would need to prevail.

347
00:21:24,480 --> 00:21:26,337
The Germans were planning
to use the ultimate

348
00:21:26,420 --> 00:21:29,560
power of immortality to conquer the world.

349
00:21:44,920 --> 00:21:46,760
I'll read the heat inside.

350
00:21:47,220 --> 00:21:48,800
The fireplace is lit.

351
00:21:49,760 --> 00:21:53,584
Four lights on the wall, two on
the ceiling, two on the desk, no.

352
00:21:54,100 --> 00:21:54,930
Three.

353
00:21:55,013 --> 00:21:56,737
Four humans standing by the wall.

354
00:21:56,820 --> 00:22:00,840
Their heights are 178, 174,

355
00:22:01,100 --> 00:22:04,480
181, and 178 centimeters.

356
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:09,520
One human is by the fireplace,
183 centimeters tall.

357
00:22:10,560 --> 00:22:13,360
There are five humans, all male.

358
00:22:25,880 --> 00:22:29,880
One, two, that's four and five.

359
00:22:35,860 --> 00:22:38,180
So you must be cars.

360
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:39,637
You're fast.

361
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:43,697
In just a few hours you heard
about your friend's defeat?

362
00:22:43,780 --> 00:22:45,917
Learned that we had obtained the stone!

363
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:48,857
Found our location and have come for it.

364
00:22:48,940 --> 00:22:50,197
Very impressive!

365
00:22:50,280 --> 00:22:53,977
And then this brutal,
perfectly calculated assault.

366
00:22:54,060 --> 00:22:58,157
Not one of my men made even the
slightest sound before they died.

367
00:22:58,240 --> 00:23:01,920
I was sure there were only
five men in this room?

368
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:06,680
Now tell me, why can't
I sense your body heat?

369
00:23:06,960 --> 00:23:08,737
Hey, rifle heads! What's...

370
00:23:08,820 --> 00:23:11,920
what's a guy gotta do to
get a little food in here?

371
00:23:12,940 --> 00:23:13,770
Cars!

372
00:23:15,380 --> 00:23:16,210
Huh?

373
00:23:16,540 --> 00:23:18,240
This man's mechanical.

374
00:23:18,740 --> 00:23:19,820
Wait a minute.

375
00:23:21,720 --> 00:23:23,480
You're von Stroheim!

376
00:23:38,600 --> 00:23:40,497
I'll take you out and out.

377
00:23:40,580 --> 00:23:43,820
I'll spend the day your way.

378
00:23:45,700 --> 00:23:48,597
Call it morning driving through the sun.

379
00:23:48,680 --> 00:23:50,280
And in and out the valley.

380
00:24:00,120 --> 00:24:03,357
The music dance and sing.

381
00:24:03,440 --> 00:24:07,537
They make the chill and drum really ring.

382
00:24:07,620 --> 00:24:11,620
I'll spend the day your way.

383
00:24:13,100 --> 00:24:15,737
Cold in morning, driving through the sun.

384
00:24:15,820 --> 00:24:17,560
And in and out the valley.

385
00:24:19,580 --> 00:24:22,160
In and out around the lake.

386
00:24:23,360 --> 00:24:25,557
Mountains come out of the sky.

387
00:24:25,640 --> 00:24:27,260
And they'll stand there.

388
00:24:30,440 --> 00:24:32,557
One mile over, we'll be there.

389
00:24:32,640 --> 00:24:34,000
And we'll see you.

390
00:24:37,020 --> 00:24:40,400
Ten and two summers, we'll
be there laughing too.

391
00:24:43,560 --> 00:24:46,137
Twenty-four, we'll fall by the real sea.

392
00:24:46,220 --> 00:24:49,220
I'll be there with you.

393
00:24:59,060 --> 00:25:00,860
We shot the tack now!

394
00:25:01,020 --> 00:25:04,497
The building on top of that hill is
the address That was pretty mean.

395
00:25:04,580 --> 00:25:07,051
German science is the finest in the world!

396
00:25:07,360 --> 00:25:08,920
No machine can stop me.
